# Command environment labels (required)

**Every** terminal command, URL, or deploy step the agent gives must state **where it runs** — never a bare command without context.

## Label taxonomy

| Label | Where | Examples |
|-------|--------|----------|
| **Local Mac (repo)** | Terminal on your Mac, inside `Assistedly.ai` | `npm run dev`, `git pull`, `npm run lint` |
| **Local Mac URL** | Browser on your Mac | `http://localhost:3010/` (port from `npm run dev`) |
| **Dev preview (tunnel)** | Cloudflare tunnel to local dev | `https://agent1.assistedly.ai/` (needs `npm run tunnel:dev` on Mac) |
| **Production / live** | Public site or origin host | `https://assistedly.ai/`, SSH `75.127.14.185` |
| **Cursor cloud workspace** | Agent VM only (not your Mac) | Paths under `/workspace`, agent-run `npm run build` |

## Format

Before each command block, one line:

- `**Local Mac (repo):**` — git, npm, sed on project files
- `**Local Mac (repo) + dev preview:**` — when both dev server and tunnel are needed
- `**Production / live (SSH):**` — full `ssh -i ~/.ssh/7-5-25kuroit opencode@HOST '…'` (see `ssh-connection-format.mdc`)
- `**Dev preview (tunnel):**` — URL only or `npm run tunnel:dev` on Mac

Do **not** say “run this command” without a label. Do **not** use production `https://assistedly.ai/` as the first preview link for unmerged work (see `cloudflare-tunnel-preview.mdc`).

## SSH

Remote steps always use the full copy-pasteable SSH one-liner with key, user, IP, and quoted remote command — labeled **Production / live (SSH)** or **Migration host (SSH)** as appropriate.
